+
+## Page headers
+
+Every app route renders `AppHeader` as its page header, new pages included. Put it first inside
+`KibanaPageTemplate`, outside the content sections:
+
+```tsx
+import { AppHeader } from '@kbn/app-header';
+import { KibanaPageTemplate } from '@kbn/shared-ux-page-kibana-template';
+
+<KibanaPageTemplate>
+  <AppHeader title={title} description={description} />
+  <KibanaPageTemplate.Section>{content}</KibanaPageTemplate.Section>
+</KibanaPageTemplate>;
+```
 
+`AppHeader` reads Chrome from context, so mount the app through `KibanaRenderContextProvider
+{...coreStart}`. Use it instead of `EuiPageHeader`, `EuiPageTemplate.Header`,
+`KibanaPageTemplate.Header` or the `pageHeader` prop; see [Migrating route
+headers](#migrating-route-headers).
+
